# `npm run build` output, with one exception.
#
# star-ui's build.rs embeds the shell document and the hashed chunks into the
# binary (spec §2.3: "one binary, no filesystem dependency at runtime, no Node
# process"), and the Rust CI job has no `setup-node` step — rust-migration.yml
# runs `cargo test` straight off the checkout. So `build/index.html` and
# `build/_app/**` are committed as the input to that embed; everything else the
# adapter writes is either a copy of `static/` (canvas, fonts, images) or not
# read by anyone.
#
# Regenerate with `npm ci && npm run build` in this directory before committing
# a source change: a stale `build/_app` means the binary serves the previous
# page set, which looks like a hydration bug rather than a build one.
build/*
!build/index.html
!build/_app
